# ── git here is for the CODE, and the RUNTIME assets that make it run. ─────
# Source art (.glb sculpts, hundreds of megabytes) stays out: it is binary,
# effectively static, does not need per-line history, and makes every git
# command crawl. Back it up separately (a drive or a cloud folder).
#
# CHANGED 2026-07-18 (user): website/assets and website/sound are now TRACKED.
# They were ignored, so a GitHub zip download arrived with no models and no
# sound and the game could not run. The runtime set is ~52 MB over ~690 files
# (.vox/.json/.mp4/moon.jpg) — fine for git. The .glb source art stays OUT:
# 369 MB in 9 files, and palm_tree.glb alone is 233 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file hard limit — including it would make the push fail outright.

# source art trees — not loaded by the game
art/
.vox/
/sound/
website_old/
website/old/
website/_snapshots/

# .glb sculpts are the source form; the game loads baked .vox instead
*.glb

# scratch
*.bak
*.log
node_modules/
